  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Andrew Christopher Currie studied natural sciences at Cambridge before spending 15 years with BP Chemicals. He moved to Inspec, the business from which INEOS emerged, taking responsibility for sales and marketing. As the new group grew through acquisitions, Currie became a director and one of the three owners alongside Jim Ratcliffe and John Reece.\n\nCurrie’s long tenure joined commercial management with a substantial minority shareholding. INEOS developed into a global chemicals and industrial group spanning petrochemicals, polymers, refining and specialist products. He now owns 19.19% of the parent and continues to serve actively on its board. That combination makes him both a long-serving operator and a durable owner of the enterprise.",
    "html": "<p>Andrew Christopher Currie studied natural sciences at Cambridge before spending 15 years with BP Chemicals. He moved to Inspec, the business from which INEOS emerged, taking responsibility for sales and marketing. As the new group grew through acquisitions, Currie became a director and one of the three owners alongside Jim Ratcliffe and John Reece.</p>\r\n<p>Currie’s long tenure joined commercial management with a substantial minority shareholding. INEOS developed into a global chemicals and industrial group spanning petrochemicals, polymers, refining and specialist products. He now owns 19.19% of the parent and continues to serve actively on its board. That combination makes him both a long-serving operator and a durable owner of the enterprise.</p>\r\n",
